# Both hostnames answered every request with 200, so every page existed twice as far as a
# search engine was concerned. www is the canonical host: it is what astro.config.mjs `site`
# declares and what every canonical and og:url tag on the site already says.
#
# The source is written with its full origin so the rule can only ever match the bare apex.
# A bare "/*" here would match www as well and loop forever.
https://seeyouiniceland.is/* https://www.seeyouiniceland.is/:splat 301

# Old Framer URLs that Bing still has indexed. Until the 404 page existed they answered with the
# home page, so they show up as duplicate titles; a 301 hands any links they carry to the cabin.
/cabins/lakeview-cabin /cabins/secluded-cabin 301
/secludedcabin /cabins/secluded-cabin 301
